## Import

Repository webhooks can be imported using the repository owner, repository name, and webhook ID in the format `owner:repo:webhook_id`.

```shell
terraform import forgejo_repository_webhook.my_webhook my-org:my-repo:123
```

To find the webhook ID, you can:
1. List webhooks via the Forgejo API: `GET /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/hooks`
2. Check the repository webhook settings in the Forgejo web interface
3. Use the Forgejo API directly with tools like `curl`:

```bash
# List all webhooks for a repository
curl -H "Authorization: token YOUR_TOKEN" \
     https://your-forgejo.com/api/v1/repos/my-org/my-repo/hooks
```

**Note:** The repository must exist before importing a webhook. When importing, Terraform will need access to the repository via the configured provider authentication.

### Import Examples

**Personal repository webhook:**
```shell
terraform import forgejo_repository_webhook.personal_webhook my-username:my-repo:456
```

**Organization repository webhook:**
```shell
terraform import forgejo_repository_webhook.org_webhook my-org:project-repo:789
```